  "analysis": "Tools available: qemu-system-x86_64, expect, nc, python3, qemu-img. No sshpass, no socat, no mkisofs/genisoimage, no 7z. Mounting the ISO failed (container lacks privileges), so I can't mount to inspect. I need to decide: (a) boot the ISO directly and hope it provides a serial console, or (b) extract vmlinuz+initramfs and boot with explicit console=ttyS0. I should check KVM availability and internet (for apk/pycdlib), then do a quick empirical boot test over a TCP serial server to see if a login prompt appears.",
  "plan": "1) Check /dev/kvm and qemu version. 2) Test internet connectivity (needed for any apk install / pip). 3) Launch qemu with a TCP serial server (blocking on connect) and connect via a small python script to capture boot output for ~25s, sending a newline to elicit a login prompt. This tells me whether direct serial boot yields a root shell. Based on that I'll choose the extraction-or-direct path.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -l /dev/kvm 2>&1; echo '---'; qemu-system-x86_64 --version 2>&1 | head -1\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import socket; s=socket.socket(); s.settimeout(5); print('net_connect=',s.connect_ex(('dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org',80)))\" 2>&1\n",
      "duration": 6.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "No /dev/kvm (qemu will use TCG software emulation — slower but functional). QEMU 5.2.0, internet works. I can't mount the ISO. I'll do an empirical boot test: launch qemu with the ISO as a CD, a virtio disk, and user-mode networking with hostfwd tcp::2222->:22, exposing the serial console over a TCP socket. Then I'll connect and see whether a root login prompt appears on the serial console. This determines whether I can configure the VM via serial or must use the kernel-extract approach.",
  "plan": "1) Launch qemu in background with -display none, serial on TCP 127.0.0.1:4555 (server,nowait), CD boot, disk, and hostfwd. 2) Write a small python client to connect and capture serial output (with the ability to send newlines) to confirm we get a login prompt. This test will reveal the serial console behavior.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "nohup qemu-system-x86_64 -m 512 -smp 2 -boot d -cdrom /app/alpine.iso -drive file=/app/alpine-disk.qcow2,format=qcow2,if=virtio -netdev user,id=net0,hostfwd=tcp::2222-:22 -device virtio-net-pci,netdev=net0 -display none -serial tcp:127.0.0.1:4555,server,nowait > /tmp/qemu.log 2>&1 &\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sleep 2; cat /tmp/qemu.log; echo '---'; ss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep 4555 || netstat -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep 4555\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    }
  ]
}

